      },
      "overview": "In an unweighted graph, BFS explores vertices in layers of increasing distance. The queue preserves that order.",
      "takeaways": [
        "Mark a vertex when you enqueue it, so it enters the queue once.",
        "The shortest-path guarantee requires equal edge costs."
      ],
